{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-on-p-modular-hecke-significance","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:on-p-modular-hecke-significance","kind":"remark","title":"Significance of the smallest modular-Hecke nimber case","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/conj-on-p-modular-hecke"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/conj-on-p-modular-hecke","tags":["surreal-numbers","nimbers","modular-hecke","significance"],"text":"on-p-modular-hecke-significance.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:on-p-modular-hecke-significance\"></a><p>Even verifying the smallest case (<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p = 2, n = 3</code>) of the <a href=\"#conj:on-p-modular-hecke\">modular Hecke <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\leftrightarrow</code> nimber correspondence</a> would be the first explicit connection between Hecke combinatorics and nim-arithmetic, and the entry point to a larger program.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals-archimedean/on-p-modular-hecke-significance.md","heading":"Remark","number":"34.3.2"}
